{% extends 'base.jinja' %}

{% block content %}
<div class="pt-24 pb-16 px-4 sm:px-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <p class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold transition-colors duration-150"
           :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">Privacy Policy</p>
        <p class="text-sm" :class="isDark ? 'text-neutral-400' : 'text-neutral-600'">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border text-sm" :class="isDark ? 'bg-neutral-900 border-neutral-800 text-neutral-300' : 'bg-white border-neutral-300 text-neutral-700'">
        Items in <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[square brackets]</span> must be completed before this policy is published. This draft is written against the UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on Personal Data Protection (PDPL) and describes how the service works today. It is not legal advice. Have a UAE-qualified lawyer check it against the current PDPL and its executive regulations.
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 text-base leading-relaxed" :class="isDark ? 'text-neutral-300' : 'text-neutral-700'">

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">1. Who we are</p>
            <p>Bibliove is operated by <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[owner's full name]</span>, trading as <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[trade name]</span> under UAE trade licence <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[licence number, issuing authority]</span>, <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[business address in the UAE]</span> (“we”, “us”). We are the controller of the personal data described below. For privacy questions and requests, contact <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[privacy contact email]</span>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">2. What we collect</p>
            <p><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address, a hash of your password (we never store the password itself), whether your email is verified, your plan, and when your account was created.</p>
            <p><strong>API keys.</strong> The name of each key and when it was created. The key itself is shown to you once and stored only as a one-way hash.</p>
            <p><strong>Usage records.</strong> For each request we accept, the time, the key used, and the number of pages processed. We use these to show your usage, to enforce plan limits, and to bill overage.</p>
            <p><strong>Documents you upload.</strong> The PDF or image you send us is stored temporarily while it is processed and is deleted afterwards. Documents may contain personal data about you or others. The extracted text is kept for 24 hours so you can collect it from the status endpoint, then removed.</p>
            <p><strong>Payment information.</strong> Payments are handled by Stripe. We do not receive or store your card number. We store your Stripe customer ID, and we record your subscription status and plan from Stripe’s notifications.</p>
            <p><strong>Technical data.</strong> Your IP address, which we use for rate limiting and in our server logs. A session cookie that keeps you signed in. Your light or dark theme choice, saved in your browser’s local storage.</p>
            <p><strong>Email.</strong> Verification codes and password reset links are sent to you by email through our email provider.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">3. Why we use it and our lawful basis</p>
            <p>Under the PDPL we process personal data only on a lawful basis. For each purpose we rely on the following:</p>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 list-disc pl-5">
                <li><strong>To provide the service</strong> (account, API, processing, usage limits and billing): performance of a contract with you, and your request that we take steps before entering into one.</li>
                <li><strong>To keep the service secure</strong> (rate limiting, protection against fraud and abuse, preventing duplicate accounts): our legitimate interest in running a safe service, which does not override your rights.</li>
                <li><strong>To meet legal duties</strong> (tax and accounting records, responding to lawful requests from authorities): compliance with a legal obligation.</li>
                <li><strong>To communicate with you about your account and security</strong>: performance of the contract and our legitimate interest in account security.</li>
                <li><strong>Marketing emails</strong>: we do not send marketing emails at present. If we do, we will ask for your consent first, and you can withdraw it at any time.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not use your data for advertising, we do not sell it, and we do not make decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects based solely on automated processing. Plan limits are applied automatically, and you can contact us if you believe a limit has been applied in error.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">4. How long we keep it</p>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-300'">
                <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                    <thead :class="isDark ? 'bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-300' : 'bg-neutral-100 text-neutral-700'">
                        <tr><th class="p-3 font-semibold">Data</th><th class="p-3 font-semibold">Kept for</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Account and API key records</td><td class="p-3">Until you delete your account</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Usage records</td><td class="p-3">Until you delete your account</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Uploaded documents</td><td class="p-3">Deleted once processing finishes</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Extracted text</td><td class="p-3">24 hours</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Reset links</td><td class="p-3">One hour</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Record that a deleted email cannot re-register (keyed hash, not the email)</td><td class="p-3">30 days, then removed</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Server logs (including IP addresses)</td><td class="p-3">[retention period]</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-t" :class="isDark ? 'border-neutral-800' : 'border-neutral-200'"><td class="p-3">Billing and tax records</td><td class="p-3">[retention period required by UAE law]</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>When you delete your account, we remove your account, API keys, usage records and billing ledger entries. Payment records held by Stripe are governed by Stripe’s own retention rules.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">5. Who we share it with</p>
            <p>We share data only with service providers who process it on our behalf, under written terms that require them to protect it, and only as needed to run the service:</p>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 list-disc pl-5">
                <li><strong>Stripe</strong> (payments and subscription billing), <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[Stripe entity and country]</span>.</li>
                <li><strong>Resend</strong> (sending verification and password reset emails), <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[Resend entity and country]</span>.</li>
                <li><strong>Aiven</strong> (database hosting), <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[hosting region]</span>.</li>
                <li><strong>[Hosting provider]</strong> (application servers and Redis), <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[region]</span>.</li>
                <li><strong>Cloudflare cdnjs</strong>, which serves icon and code libraries to your browser. Loading these shares your IP address with Cloudflare.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We may also disclose data where UAE law requires it, including to competent authorities. We will not sell your personal data.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">6. Transfers outside the UAE</p>
            <p>Some of our providers are located outside the UAE, including in the United States and Europe. Under the PDPL we transfer personal data outside the UAE only where the destination country provides an adequate level of protection, or where we have appropriate contractual safeguards with the recipient. <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[Confirm, for each provider, which basis applies and keep the contract on file.]</span> Where the law permits a transfer on another basis, such as your consent, we will tell you before we rely on it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">7. Cookies and similar technologies</p>
            <p>We use only what the service needs. A session cookie keeps you signed in and protects our forms against cross-site request forgery. Your theme choice is stored in your browser’s local storage. We do not use advertising or analytics cookies.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">8. Security and breach notification</p>
            <p>We hash passwords and API keys, protect forms against forged requests, rate-limit requests, verify payment notifications by signature, and restrict access to our systems. <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[Describe encryption in transit and at rest once production hosting is configured.]</span> No system is completely secure, so please use a strong, unique password and keep your API keys private.</p>
            <p>If a personal data breach is likely to put your rights and freedoms at risk, we will notify the UAE Data Office and the affected individuals within the time limits set by the PDPL and its executive regulations, and we will describe what happened and what we are doing about it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">9. Your rights</p>
            <p>Under the PDPL you have the right to:</p>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 list-disc pl-5">
                <li>be informed about how we process your data (this policy);</li>
                <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
                <li>have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected or updated;</li>
                <li>have your data erased, which you can do yourself from Settings;</li>
                <li>receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format, where the PDPL provides for it;</li>
                <li>restrict our processing, or object to it, in the circumstances the PDPL sets out;</li>
                <li>withdraw consent at any time, where we rely on consent;</li>
                <li>lodge a complaint with the UAE Data Office.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>To exercise these rights, email <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[privacy contact email]</span>. We will respond within <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[response period under the PDPL executive regulations]</span>. We may ask you to confirm your identity first, and we may refuse a request where the PDPL allows it, in which case we will tell you why.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">10. Children</p>
            <p>Bibliove is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[age under the PDPL and UAE law]</span>, and where the PDPL requires a guardian’s consent for a child’s data, we will obtain it before processing. If you believe a child has given us data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">11. Changes to this policy</p>
            <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date above and, for material changes, tell you by email or in the service before the change takes effect.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <p class="text-xl font-bold" :class="isDark ? 'text-white' : 'text-black'">12. Governing law and contact</p>
            <p>This policy is governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates. Questions about it: <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[privacy contact email]</span>, <span class="font-mono text-orange-600">[business address]</span>.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
